14. What are time complexity and space complexity?

Time complexity: Measures how an algorithm's execution time grows with the input size.

Space complexity: Measures how much memory an algorithm requires as the input size grows.

15. Explain Big-O, Omega and Theta notations.

These notations describe the growth rate of an algorithm's time or space requirements.

Big-O O: Represents an asymptotic upper bound.

Omega Ω: Represents an asymptotic lower bound.

Theta Θ: Represents a tight asymptotic bound (both upper and lower).

